                        <format attr='margin' value='8' />
                        <format attr='padding' value='8' />
                      </zone-style>
                    </zone>
                    <zone h='34301' id='23' name='Predicted default rates match actual rates across risk deciles' w='49430' x='49999' y='15999'>
                      <zone-style>
                        <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                        <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                        <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                        <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                      </zone-style>
                    </zone>
                    <zone forceUpdate='true' h='17600' id='29' type-v2='text' w='49430' x='49999' y='81600'>
                      <formatted-text>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Illustrative assumptions: 15% </run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>profit on repaid loans, </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>60%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> loss on defaults. Darker bar = recommended cutoff.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Approval cutoff:</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> approve an applicant if their predicted default risk is below this value.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Recommendation: </run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>approve applicants whose predicted default risk is under </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>20%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>. That approves about </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>65% </run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>of applicants at a </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>12%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> default rate (vs. </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>18.8%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> if everyone is approved) and avoids about 58% of defaults. Under illustrative assumptions (</run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>15%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> profit on repaid loans, </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>60%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> loss on defaults), profit peaks at this cutoff, about </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>4.3x </run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>what approving everyone would earn. A risk-averse lender could tighten to </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>0.15</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>, which approves about </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>46%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> of applicants at a </run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>10%</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'> default rate.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial'>Importance = drop in model accuracy (AUC) when a feature is randomly shuffled. Closely related features share credit, so loan size, income ratios, and term overlap.</run>
                      </formatted-text>
                      <zone-style>
                        <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                        <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                        <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                        <format attr='margin' value='4' />
